Package: proton-drive-sync-engine
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         libwebkit2gtk-4.1-0,
         libsoup-3.0-0,
         libgtk-3-0
Recommends: libsecret-tools
Suggests: proton-sync-nautilus, proton-sync-nemo
Description: two-way file sync engine and desktop GUI for Proton Drive
 Bidirectionally synchronizes a local folder with Proton Drive. Ships:
 .
  * proton-syncd  — the background sync daemon (systemd user service)
  * proton-sync   — a control CLI that talks to the daemon over a
                     Unix socket (status, activity, dry-run review)
  * proton-sync-gui — a Tauri desktop GUI for status, activity,
                     conflict resolution, dry-run review, and settings
 .
 This package does NOT bundle the proprietary `proton-drive` command-line
 client published by Proton. You must install it yourself and make sure
 it is on PATH: proton-syncd shells out to it for every remote Proton
 Drive operation and reads its cached session from the desktop keyring
 (see the libsecret-tools recommendation, which provides secret-tool).
 .
 Optional per-file sync-status emblems for the Nautilus and Nemo file
 managers are packaged separately as proton-sync-nautilus and
 proton-sync-nemo.

Package: proton-sync-nautilus
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3, python3-nautilus
Enhances: proton-drive-sync-engine
Description: Nautilus file-manager emblems for Proton Drive Sync
 Adds per-file sync-status emblems (synced / syncing / conflict) to the
 GNOME Files (Nautilus) file manager by reading proton-syncd's local
 SQLite index read-only. Requires proton-drive-sync-engine's daemon to
 have populated an index; this is a cosmetic enhancement only and is
 never the sole signal of sync state.
 .
 Restart Nautilus after installing: nautilus -q

Package: proton-sync-nemo
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3, nemo-python | python3-nemo
Enhances: proton-drive-sync-engine
Description: Nemo file-manager emblems for Proton Drive Sync
 Adds per-file sync-status emblems (synced / syncing / conflict) to the
 Cinnamon Nemo file manager by reading proton-syncd's local SQLite index
 read-only. Requires proton-drive-sync-engine's daemon to have populated
 an index; this is a cosmetic enhancement only and is never the sole
 signal of sync state.
